{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9e3b9745aa61a48a","name":"Near-Human","source":{"id":"source:reference-9e3b9745aa61a48a","title":"Near-Human","revision":26005,"timestamp":"2025-01-15T03:24:09Z","sha256":"4ba1819ed4a1d53278f86a189cddde951261dca32cc6b37ca92bc74dcdd1b47f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26005","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Near-Human&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9e3b9745aa61a48a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Throughout much of the galaxy, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"}," are the most commonly encountered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},". Not surprisingly, after a millennium of interstellar travel and colonization, an enormous number of humanoids share a common genetic code. Commonly called Near-Humans, these humanoids are substantially the same as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"}," in look and physiology, but exhibit one or more differences significant enough to set them apart. The origins of most Near-Humans are not known, but the common assumption is that isolated groups naturally adapt to the specific environmental conditions of their current world.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["These conditions occasionally cause genetic mutations, improving the Near-Humans' likelihood of survival. However, genetic engineering and cloning technology are other possible explanations for Near-Humans' variation from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," norms. Classification efforts are further complicated by the many bipedal humanoid ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," that are unrelated to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"},". Looks can be deceiving.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars Roleplaying Game Saga Edition"]},", Near-Humans have only small differences from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"},". These differences might be cosmetic, physiological, or, most commonly, both. Players and Gamemasters wanting to create their own Near-Human characters should use the following Near-Human generation system.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Creating Near-Humans"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["To create a Near-Human, start with the base ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," Species. Next, select one of the traits from the Near-Human Traits table below, replacing either the bonus ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained Skill"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained_Skill"}," or the bonus ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"}," that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"}," normally receive. Finally, select one, two, or three minor physiological variations from the Near-Human Variants table below. These variants are typically cosmetic, but Gamemasters might allow a variant to have a minor mechanical roleplaying effect. Variants normally should not cause a Near-Human character to incur a penalty to attack rolls or skill checks, but it might occasionally do so at the Gamemaster's discretion. As always, the Gamemaster has the final say in trait and variant combinations allowed in his or her game.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Traits"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Select one of the traits from the Near-Human Traits table below, replacing either the bonus ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained Skill"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained_Skill"}," or the bonus ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"}," that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"}," normally receive.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TRAIT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DESCRIPTION\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Ability Adjustment\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Increase one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Score"}," by 2 and reduce another by 2 to account for emphasis in certain attributes (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"},").\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Additional Arms\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Up to 2 additional arms. When making multiple attacks, the character can reduce the penalty to the attack roll by 2.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Biotech Augmentation\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Augmented with biotechnology. Select one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bio-Implant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bio-Implant"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Breathe Underwater\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Amphibious and cannot drown in water. Can have gill slits or similar external features.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Climate Adaptation\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Resistant to a specific climate. Select one: freezing, rarefied atmosphere, searing, smoky, tropical, or watery. When challenged by an environmental factor in that climate (chosen from those listed, or others at the Gamemaster's discretion), can reroll an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endurance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endurance","referenceId":"reference:98c8abf84e23ff3f"}," or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Survival"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Survival","referenceId":"reference:8302496de0ace160"}," check, taking the better result.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Conductive\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Naturally generate a small amount of electrical energy and use as a Natural Weapon in an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unarmed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unarmed"}," attack, dealing 1d6 points of Energy damage. Character is always considered armed with a Natural Weapon.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Cultural Cybernetics\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Culture commonly augments members with cybernetics from birth. Select one cybernetic enhancement.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Darkvision\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," (including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Total Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Total_Concealment"},") from darkness. However, you cannot perceive colors in total darkness.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Empath\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Telepathy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Telepathy"}," application of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," skill ",{"tag":"a","children":["Untrained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Untrained"},", and without having the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Sensitivity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Sensitivity","referenceId":"reference:5202cab02f367bcf"}," feat. Additionally, can sense the emotions of a target if the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check equals or exceeds the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Expert Swimmer\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can reroll a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"}," check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Can ",{"tag":"a","children":["Take 10"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Take_10"}," on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"}," checks when distracted or threatened.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Heightened Awareness\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can reroll a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Low-Light Vision\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," (but not ",{"tag":"a","children":["Total Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Total_Concealment"},") from darkness.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Natural Armor\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Thickened skin or natural armor plates grant a Natural Armor bonus of +1 to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Natural Weapon\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can use natural claws in an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unarmed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unarmed"}," attack, dealing 1d6 points of Slashing damage instead of normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unarmed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unarmed"}," damage. Character is always considered armed with the Natural Weapons.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Naturally Acrobatic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," skill, even if it is not normally a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Class Skill"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Class_Skill"}," for the character.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Persistent\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Can reroll a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endurance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endurance","referenceId":"reference:98c8abf84e23ff3f"}," check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Quick\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Increases base ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," by 1 square.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Quick Healing\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["At the end of an encounter, regain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," equal to 1d4 + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," modifier (minimum 1).\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Resistant\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Naturally resistant to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poisons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poisons"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Diseases"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Diseases"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Radiation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Radiation","referenceId":"reference:669c428e617d7f09"},", or other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hazards"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hazards"},", gaining a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},". Gamemaster can restrict resistance to a single, specific ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hazard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hazard"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Scent\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["At close range (within 10 squares), ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concealment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concealment"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cover"}," for purposes of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," checks, and take no penalty from poor visibility when using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Track"}," application of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Survival"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Survival","referenceId":"reference:8302496de0ace160"}," skill.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Spring Step\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["When using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["High Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/High_Jump"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Long Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Long_Jump"}," applications of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump","referenceId":"reference:9ee0ca3e24d60ea0"}," skill, reduce the number of squares required for a running start by 2.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Strength Surge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Once per encounter, can reroll one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"},"-based ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Check"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"},", doubling the character's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," modifier (minimum +1), or can add 2 to a single damage roll on a successful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"},", when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," normally adds to the roll. This does not apply when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Finesse"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Finesse","referenceId":"reference:7752dd7b768faff2"}," is used.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Visually Striking\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Character's appearance is visually surprising or stunning. The character's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charisma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charisma"}," bonus is doubled when using the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}," skill on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"},", Near-Humans, and similar humanoids (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'leks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27leks"},").\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Weapon Familiarity\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Character selects a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"}," and treats it as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapon"}," instead. Must be commonly used by character's native culture.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Variants"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["These variants are typically cosmetic, but Gamemasters might allow a variant to have a minor mechanical roleplaying effect. Variants normally should not cause a Near-Human character to incur a penalty to attack rolls or skill checks, but it might occasionally do so at the Gamemaster's discretion. As always, the Gamemaster has the final say in trait and variant combinations allowed in his or her game.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["VARIATION\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DESCRIPTION\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Eye Variation\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Eyes are of an unusual color and/or pupils are of an unusual shape.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Digit Variation\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Number of digits on each hand or foot is greater or fewer than 5, but without affecting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill"}," use in terms of game mechanics.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Fins\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Character has small fins that have no effect on swimming.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Hair Variation\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Character's hair is naturally an unusual color, length, texture, or size.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Shaped\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Character has been biologically altered by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yuuzhan Vong"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong","referenceId":"reference:93079e2f7d73d480"}," shaping process. This can account for the character's Near-Human Trait, or the trait might be cosmetic or for roleplaying purposes. Shaped characters typically gain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yuuzhan Vong"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong","referenceId":"reference:93079e2f7d73d480"}," physical features or are otherwise physically altered.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Skin Color\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Skin is naturally a color (or a combination of colors) not normally associated with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Skin Texture\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Obviously unusual skin texture, such as leathery, especially smooth, overly wrinkled, or scaly.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Teeth Variation\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Teeth are noticeably differently colored, sharper, larger, or smaller than those of typical ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Towering\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Over 2 meters tall, although the additional height does not change the character's Size.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Webbed Digits\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Flaps of skin span the character's fingers or toes.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
